{"author":{"id":"40e3ba2788b3b9fc163c354afc44e5f9d225bcf0a27e679aaa878dd6135c6dcb"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793918764,"nonce":"L+OUtFlI6sYs63RNZT3v2H5pOe4=","message":"Implemented the Linux read-only uc2-mount entry point in alpha5. Newest entries are under /files and stored versions under /versions/N. Verified decoded-file LRU cache is bounded by bytes and entries; each decode gets a fresh bounded-master reader. Source changes return ESTALE, corrupt entries are not cached, writes are refused. Eight unit tests plus a real FUSE mount passed: four files, a stored version, 16 concurrent random reads, and forced eviction with a 1 MiB / one-file cache. Documentation: docs/mount.md; release evidence: docs/releases/3.0.0a5-qa.md. Implementation is committed on the alpha5 branch; publication is being completed.","files":null}]}